From 1cecfc59558f11dfea2023691c23e1331053426d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:13:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/61] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon, NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT is an
 uncached allocation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NVK means an uncached map by HOST_COHERENT on an SoC — it says so where
it advertises the two memory types (nvk_physical_device.c:1571-1575) —
and NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT is what carries that down. Cache maintenance
cannot stand in for it: nvkmd_mem_sync_to_gpu and sync_from_gpu return
before doing anything when the flag is set (nvkmd.c:457, :476), so a
cached allocation behind that flag would get no maintenance from
anywhere and neither side would see the other's writes.

horizon_gpu gained HORIZON_GPU_MEM_UNCACHED for exactly this (D14);
this is the call site. Everything else stays CACHED, which is what heap
memory is and what the explicit flush/invalidate around it expects.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — decision D14, taken by the owner
Why: Vulkan requires a HOST_VISIBLE + HOST_COHERENT memory type, so it
  cannot be dropped, and with only a cached policy it was a promise the
  platform could not keep.
Evidence: nvkmd.c:457 and :476 return early on NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT.
Upstream: no — this is the Horizon backend's own allocator.
---
 .../vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c  | 27 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
index cfcc923..772234e 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_mem.c
@@ -189,17 +189,26 @@ nvkmd_horizon_alloc_mem(struct nvkmd_dev *_dev,
    if (align != 0 && align < HORIZON_GPU_SMALL_PAGE_SIZE)
       align = HORIZON_GPU_SMALL_PAGE_SIZE;
 
-   /* HORIZON_GPU_MEM_CACHED is the only policy horizon_gpu offers, and
-    * that is a statement about the platform rather than a limitation of
-    * this backend: homebrew heap memory on Horizon is CPU-cached.
-    * NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT therefore cannot be satisfied by the allocation
-    * itself — it is satisfied by the sync_to_gpu/sync_from_gpu calls
-    * nvk already makes around every access, which is decision D5 and is
-    * why that decision is still open.
+   /* NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT means what NVK says it means on an SoC: an
+    * *uncached* map, the alternative to the cached one
+    * (nvk_physical_device.c:1571-1575). It cannot be satisfied by cache
+    * maintenance instead, because nvkmd_mem_sync_to_gpu and
+    * sync_from_gpu return before doing anything when the flag is set
+    * (nvkmd.c:457, :476) — so a cached allocation behind that flag
+    * would get no maintenance from anywhere and neither side would see
+    * the other's writes.
+    *
+    * D14. horizon_gpu gained the policy for exactly this; everything
+    * else stays CACHED, which is what heap memory is and what the
+    * explicit flush/invalidate around it expects.
     */
+   const horizon_gpu_cache_policy policy =
+      (flags & NVKMD_MEM_COHERENT) ? HORIZON_GPU_MEM_UNCACHED
+                                   : HORIZON_GPU_MEM_CACHED;
+
    horizon_gpu_result res =
-      horizon_gpu_mem_create(dev->gpu, size_B, align,
-                             HORIZON_GPU_MEM_CACHED, &mem->gpu_mem);
+      horizon_gpu_mem_create(dev->gpu, size_B, align, policy,
+                             &mem->gpu_mem);
    if (res.status != HORIZON_GPU_OK) {
       FREE(mem);
       return vk_errorf(log_obj, nvkmd_horizon_result(res),
-- 
